+# Kart handling refinements — 2026-10-30
+
+KR01: The owner prefers the current kart handling to the earlier test alternatives. Keep the `kart-7` resource as the reference and replace the five kart experiments with five refinements. KR02: Keep the race-view selector and practice/result safeguards, and preserve other cars' options.
+
+The five choices start from an independent duplicate of the current kart config. **Quick** increases steering buildup; **Tight** adds steering lock and reduces high-speed steering reduction; **Flow** retains a little more speed through a bend; **Brake turn** adds controlled braking rotation; **Playful** permits a little more slip. The five earlier kart experiments are removed. Current handling remains in the dropdown for a direct comparison. The engine, brakes, speed limit, dimensions and kart-specific controls are unchanged. Test setups receive new identities and remain practice-only; they do not change canonical records or online contracts. Other cars' presets are untouched.
+
+With the pinned Godot 4.7.2 build and isolated local profiles:
+
+- `--headless --path game --script res://tests/test_kart_handling_refinements.gd`: 22 checks, zero failures. Compared with current handling in specific sampled maneuvers, Quick builds steering 35.7% faster at three ticks; Tight adds 4.64° heading after a one-second powered turn; Flow retains 0.086 m/s more in that turn; Brake turn adds 1.97° heading in a half-second braking turn; Playful's peak slip rises from 5.64° to 7.89°. All five retain the same measured straight acceleration and specified power, braking and speed limit. These are sample measurements, not a claim about human feel or lap performance.
+- `--headless --path game --script res://tests/test_handling_test_presets.gd`: zero failures; sampled turning distinguishes the choices, remains finite, replays identically and recovers after steering release. The retained test also exercises other cars and Compact.
+- `--headless --path game --script res://tests/test_handling_test_selector.gd`: 39 checks, zero failures, including the new names and all other car selectors.
+- `--headless --path game --script res://tests/test_handling_test_integration.gd`: 16 checks, zero failures, including restart and practice fences. `res://tests/test_handling_test_app.gd`: four checks, zero failures, including ticket retirement and no personal-best or upload for a test run.
+- `--headless --path game --script res://tests/test_kart.gd`: 42 checks, zero failures, on the unchanged current kart.
+- `--path game --rendering-method gl_compatibility --script res://tests/capture_kart_handling_refinements.gd`: zero failures. Actual kart race, mouse-opened menu and selection at 960×540 and 1280×720; [open menu](evidence/kart-handling-refinements-2026-10-30/race-open-960x540.png). Captures use an isolated profile and `BMT_HANDLING_TEST_CAPTURE` output directory.
+
+The offline runs emitted a Windows certificate-store warning. The simulation tests also reported resources still in use at exit, and the graphical capture logged hitches. The modes still need owner driving-feel assessment; touch and physical-device testing were not performed. No APK, owner-save write, backend deployment, or owner-process restart was performed.
